  "brief": 242,
  "observations": "The healthy and type 1 islets register at equal square display size. Their opaque silhouette IoU is 99.79%, and their horizontal and vertical centroids differ by under 0.5 px on the 2,000 px comparison canvas. Use the scene 3 swap. The water glass and urine jar have visible edges on cream. The can and full-size thermometer have no printed text or numerals.\n\nThe starting particle counts and ideal 30/30 and 24/24 water splits recalculate. In six sample runs of the existing engine, the raw late normal readout ranged from −5 to 14 and the diabetes readout from −10 to 10. The model did not reliably hold the intended near-6 and near-0 comparison. Record the design's named steady count-bar fallback for build. Keep both values labelled as relative model counts. Evidence in `work/brief242/fa2-v32-20-nov/tubule-engine-check.json`.",
